add('knowno','INSPECTED CODE: The official google-research/language_model_uncertainty release consists of three executable notebooks and README. MobileManipulation cells23–27 explicitly temperature-scale the five option scores (temperature5), use minimum nonconformity across acceptable labels, compute the finite-sample corrected quantile, and include options above1-qhat. Its test loop sets simulated task success equal to set coverage and assumes the human always selects a correct included option; help triggers for non-singletons and the extra option. This precisely supports the stated ideal-human assumption, not physical execution reliability or conditional error control among autonomous actions. The demo uses a stored threshold; tabletop notebook includes PyBullet manipulation primitives and separate calibration. No notebook cells, API calls or physical/simulated controller were executed. Proprietary original model weights and real robot deployment are outside the release.', ['language_model_uncertainty/KnowNo_Demo.ipynb: prediction-set cells','language_model_uncertainty/KnowNo_MobileManipulation.ipynb: cells23–27 (extracted text373–481)','language_model_uncertainty/KnowNo_TabletopSim.ipynb: environment reset/motion and calibration references'])
add('babywalk','INSPECTED CODE: src/follower.py:149–202 reconstructs prior subtask context and combines history embeddings using L1-normalized exponential recency weights, default decay0.5; negative decay selects learned LSTM memory. This is an explicit forgetting inductive bias, not perfect retention. Sequential inference starts each new subtask at the previous executed endpoint and heading and appends its realized history (486–548). The training driver branches among imitation, reward training and curriculum RL; it advances curriculum and resets optimizers at the configured interval (train_follower.py:50–82,156–194). process_data.py constructs period/landmark chunks and curriculum tasks; no new VLM is involved. Assets and Matterport simulator were not loaded. Inspected source supports the staged mechanism, not independently reproduced long-route scores.', ['src/follower.py:49–115,149–202,486–548','src/train_follower.py:50–82,156–194','src/process_data.py: make_data and curriculum split dispatch'])
add('activevig','INSPECTED CODE: active/agent.py:293–343 constructs training reward/labels by comparing action outcomes with simulator goal distances and restoring the simulation state. exploration:346–415 maintains already-explored candidate masks, an exploration policy and a default four-step lookahead; greedy evaluation is explicit. These oracle distances are training supervision, not an independently calibrated confidence estimate. late_action_taking:1893–1923 removes repeated visits and reconstructs connections through stored graph paths; this supports the paper’s separate delayed-execution protocol and should not be mixed with online physical exploration costs. The train path clips gradients and steps encoder/decoder/explorer optimizers. No project source was executed, and an exhaustive replay accounting audit was not performed.', ['active/agent.py:293–415,1724–1794,1893–1923'])
add('aiuta','INSPECTED CODE: vlfm/brain/llm_brain_history.py:159–183 computes normalized entropy over exactly three yes/no/uncertain token probabilities, with an optional offset, and labels responses using a threshold. The object policy passes tau0.75 and offset0.05 for false-positive filtering, rejecting no, uncertain and do-not-know responses (base_objectnav_policy.py:408–446). The LLM alignment/question routine parses YAML similarity_score and questions, conditioned on stored facts (llm_brain_history.py:234–259). This verifies model-score thresholding and prompted questions rather than a learned or conformally calibrated error probability. The released policy inherits VLFM and pretrained PointNav; training-free refers to AIUTA’s added decision logic. API calls and Habitat navigation were not executed; model/version/prompt dependence remains a reproduction prerequisite.', ['vlfm/brain/llm_brain_history.py:159–183,234–259','vlfm/policy/base_objectnav_policy.py:408–446'])
add('ieve','INSPECTED CODE: agents/instance_exp.py loads DISK/LightGlue and implements the hand-crafted instance_discriminator switch. At629–660, >100 matches confirms a target; at goal distance<150 map units, >60 matches confirms while lower counts reject; farther candidates become temporary verification goals. An alternate instance_discriminator_auto path uses a learned switch, so its behavior must not be conflated with the hand-crafted path. main.py constructs the exploration PPO agent, loads policy weights and records success/SPL/distance at evaluation. The controller implements velocity actions; README explicitly notes the release was updated to match the paper’s velocity-control setting. No weights or Habitat evaluation were executed. Image-instance matching and threshold selection do not imply instruction-level error diagnosis.', ['README.md','agents/instance_exp.py:73–74,426–486,592–661','main.py:246–278,396–402'])
add('embodiedqa','INSPECTED CODE: training/models.py:1100–1173 runs a question-conditioned recurrent planner and gathers its hidden state for the controller, which takes image, action embedding and planner state; planner_step/controller_step separate inference calls. train_eqa.py:683–725 evaluates the last five images with the answerer, appends answer-accuracy reward, discounts returns by0.99, subtracts a running reward baseline and forms planner/controller policy losses. README warns the released shortest paths were updated because the earlier grid paths were inaccurate, so data version must be fixed for replication. The archived repository requires the House3D/SUNCG assets and older PyTorch APIs. None of these external assets or training loops was executed; current physical-world reproducibility is not established by a code snapshot.', ['README.md','training/models.py:1100–1173','training/train_eqa.py:683–725'])
add('iqa','INSPECTED CODE: networks/qa_planner_network.py constructs question-conditioned memory crops and answer/planning heads. answer_loss:220–243 uses sigmoid cross-entropy for existence/spatial answers and softmax cross-entropy for counting; move_loss:245–252 adds a ten-weighted sigmoid loss for all possible moves when enabled. This confirms auxiliary action-validity supervision in addition to question answering and RL, not an instruction-language-only learner. The release includes TensorFlow/A3C training, supervised map/navigation training, AI2-THOR interaction, question generation and evaluation entry points. Their existence is not a claim each simulator transition was audited. No simulator, training or evaluation was executed; legacy THOR/vision-model assets are prerequisites.', ['networks/qa_planner_network.py:50–79,114–189,220–253','Pinned tree: training/evaluation and question-generation entry points'])
add('embodiedgap','INSPECTED CODE: The author project links the maintained InternNav repository; the inspected pin is a current framework snapshot, not a verified historical paper release. internnav/trainer/rdp_trainer.py:109–145 implements diffusion noise/sample MSE plus progress and stop-progress MSE with configured stop loss weight. internnav/agent/rdp_agent.py:300–352 uses no_grad recurrent denoising, caches an action chunk, pops actions sequentially and returns evaluator action records. This supports chunked diffusion control and explicit stopping supervision. The framework also contains newer unrelated agents; no claims about those were inferred from this inspection. Exact paper checkpoint/config equivalence, controller latency and hardware transfer were not executed.', ['internnav/trainer/rdp_trainer.py:109–145','internnav/agent/rdp_agent.py:300–352','README.md and author project link'])
add('vlnmme','INSPECTED CODE: src/agents/baseline_agent.py:41–145 parses an Action field, gives numeric action matches priority, maps direction words to the first matching available candidate, checks navigability and handles Stop. Therefore textual formatting, option multiplicity and parsing are part of the measured agent pipeline. src/utils/eval.py implements graph nDTW with three-metre normalization and endpoint success. The repository exposes separate baseline, CoT, reflection and MapGPT agents; these are API/model inference strategies rather than a VLN-MME training method. Dataset construction and caption/oracle condition parity still require frozen annotations and configurations. No model/API/simulator execution or full cross-agent behavioral equivalence test was performed.', ['src/agents/baseline_agent.py:1–145','src/utils/eval.py:5–40','Pinned agent strategy tree'])
add('omniagent','INSPECTED CODE: verl/trainer/ppo/core_algos.py:950–989 computes each trajectory’s masked mean token entropy, divides it by the group mean entropy and broadcasts detached weights over tokens. ray_trainer.py:1392–1409 stores these weights under entropy_weights when the corresponding configuration is enabled; a distinct soft-weight option exists and must not be confused with TAURA. Mean-one trajectory weights do not prove unchanged token-weighted gradients or constant optimizer-step magnitude. The release supplies video action parsing/environment, rewards, multimodal rollout and SFT/RL framework code. The source snapshot is newer maintained code with optional reward/weight variants; paper-equivalent configuration must be frozen. No models, video inference or training were run. This is video-tool reasoning, not a physical navigation benchmark.', ['verl/trainer/ppo/core_algos.py:950–989','verl/trainer/ppo/ray_trainer.py:1380–1418','agent_system/environments/env_package/video_env.py: inspected action/reward entry-point definitions'])
